## Summary

The bug was an off-by-one error in `src/parse.py:4`. The function was returning `parts[1]` (the second word) instead of `parts[0]` (the first word). This caused:
- `test_basic` to fail because 'hello world' returned 'world' instead of 'hello'
- `test_single` to error because 'solo' only has one element, but the code tried to access index 1

The fix was simple: changed `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`, and now all tests pass successfully.
